  "failure_location": "objective",
  "root_cause_hypothesis": "The optimizer lacks an explicit deterministic safety-margin objective and nominal_performance currently contributes relatively strongly; as a result many designs are close to the failure boundary (leading to large nominal→robust drop) and noisy MC estimates (16-sample) can mislead selection.",
  "intervention_target": "objective",
  "rationale": "Observed gap: nominal mean = 0.6204 vs robust mean = 0.4602 (robust is limiting). Robust objectives are noisy (16-sample MC) and current objectives provide no deterministic incentive to increase distance from the failure boundary. Adding cliff_margin (deterministic signed distance to x0+x1=1) with modest weight will give a clear, low-noise signal to move designs away from the cliff; reducing nominal_performance weight will avoid rewarding designs that sit close to the boundary. This is a conservative, focused edit expected to improve true robust performance without changing noisy MC scorers. Quoted evidence: nominal mean 0.6204, robust mean 0.4602, best robust ≈ 0.5189, robust std 0.0342.",
