Brief reasoning: the analyzer shows the optimizer pushed designs away from the cliff (cliff_margin mean +0.0468 to 0.1194 ±0.0510) at the cost of nominal performance (nominal mean fell by 0.0578 to 0.5626 ±0.0819) while robust_performance_mc (weight=2.5) remained essentially flat (0.4565 ±0.0735). This pattern suggests the objective weighting is misaligned with the true goal (maximize expected robust performance under noise) and that search would benefit from stronger emphasis on the noisy robust estimator plus an explicit center-bias to reduce sensitivity to isotropic parameter noise.

